/F2 13 Tf (Mirelle-1 Mission Overview) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
/F2 13 Tf (1. Objectives) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(Mirelle-1 will monitor harmful algal blooms in coastal lagoons and estuaries with a) Tj T*
(six-band multispectral imager at a ground sampling distance of 30 metres. Its data will) Tj T*
(give regional fisheries agencies an early warning of blooms that can close shellfish) Tj T*
(beds, at a fraction of the cost of aerial surveys.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf (2. Orbit) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(The spacecraft will fly in a sun-synchronous orbit at 520 km altitude with the local) Tj T*
(time of the ascending node \(LTAN\) at 10:30. This gives consistent lighting for the) Tj T*
(imager and revisits each target lagoon every three days.) Tj T*
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
