/F2 13 Tf (3. Spacecraft bus) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(The bus is a six-unit aluminium structure carrying the payload, power, radio and) Tj T*
(computing units described below.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf (3.1 Attitude determination and control) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(Three reaction wheels and three magnetorquers control attitude, guided by a star) Tj T*
(tracker, six coarse sun sensors and a magnetometer. Pointing accuracy is 0.5 degrees in) Tj T*
(imaging mode, and the magnetorquers dump momentum from the wheels once per orbit.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf (3.2 On-board computer and storage) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(The on-board computer runs the flight software on a radiation-tolerant microcontroller) Tj T*
(with 32 GB of flash storage for images, enough for about four days of observations if) Tj T*
(ground contact is lost.) Tj T*
T*
ET
endstream
